date: 2026-10-19T00:00:00-04:00
---

Phlogiston is a fuel taken from the ground. Mining downward is only the first step of the work; the phlogiston is not pulled straight from the earth as it lies, and the extraction that follows is exacting enough that those who want it in quantity deal with people who know the trade rather than learn it themselves.

It comes up from the ground as a red sand and will not sit long in the open, so it is drawn off and packed into sealed barrels lined with metal to be carried. The works at [[Geography/Hesperid 3|Hesperid 3]] were raised to refine it and rail the barrels north to the [[Geography/Hesperid|Hesperid]]. A single barrel set into a rack brings a locomotive's lights and dash to life. Stored in quantity the fuel is a hazard.
